\section{Changes made}{

The data was collected to compare observers, not to survey the seabed, and
was changed as follows by \code{data-raw/bodc_data.R}:
\itemize{
\item Only Observer 1's finds in the interobserver comparison are kept, with
the labels given by the independent reviewer.
\item Each annotation is counted as one individual, and the annotations are
turned into counts per image and label.
\item Labels in the label set that were never used are kept as columns of 0.
Four labels used in the annotations are not in the published label set.
They are kept too, and marked in \code{bodc_labels.csv}.
\item Survey and date and time (from the image file name) are added to the
metadata.
}
}

\section{Limits}{

\itemize{
\item No image areas are published, so each image is given an area of 1 m².
Density is individuals per image, and SUs are built by number of images.
\item Only images with at least one annotation are in the data, so there are
no empty images. Real surveys have many, so CVs here are lower and fewer
SUs are needed than in a real survey.
\item The data is used as one stratum.
}
}

